        "text": "14"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "16"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "24"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count neighbouring faces",
        "body": "Each of the 12 sides of the 12-gon is an edge shared with another face. Two different faces of a polyhedron cannot share two edges along the 12-gon (two adjacent faces meet in a single edge), so there are at least 12 further faces: at least $1 + 12 = 13$ faces.\n\nA pyramid over a 12-gon has exactly 13 faces (the base and 12 triangles), so 13 is possible.\n\n**Answer: (B) 13**"
      }
    ],
