    "points": 4,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Assume that $x^2 - y^2 = 84$, where $x$ and $y$ are positive integers. How many values may the expression $x^2 + y^2$ have?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "6"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Factor",
        "body": "$(x - y)(x + y) = 84$. The two factors have the same parity (their sum is $2x$), and their product is even, so both are even: $(x-y, x+y) \\in \\{(2, 42), (6, 14)\\}$ (with $x - y < x + y$ and $y > 0$).\n\n- $(2, 42)$: $x = 22$, $y = 20$, $x^2 + y^2 = 884$.\n- $(6, 14)$: $x = 10$, $y = 4$, $x^2 + y^2 = 116$.\n\nTwo values.\n\n**Answer: (B) 2**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Halve the factors",
        "body": "Write $x - y = 2u$, $x + y = 2v$; then $uv = 21$ with $u < v$: $(1, 21)$ or $(3, 7)$. Each gives one pair $(x, y) = (u+v, v-u)$, namely $(22, 20)$ and $(10, 4)$, with different values of $x^2 + y^2$ ($884$ and $116$).\n\n**Answer: (B) 2**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
