    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)$, $x \\in \\mathbb R$, be the function defined by the following properties: $f$ is periodic with period 5 and $f(x) = x^2$ when $x \\in [-2, 3)$. What is $f(2013)$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "0"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "9"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Shift into the interval",
        "body": "$2013 = 5\\cdot 403 - 2$, so by periodicity $f(2013) = f(-2)$, and $-2$ lies in $[-2, 3)$: $f(-2) = 4$.\n\n(Careful: $2013 \\equiv 3 \\pmod 5$, but $3$ is *not* in $[-2, 3)$, so we must use $-2$ instead of $3$ — the answer is not 9.)\n\n**Answer: (D) 4**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "functional-equations",
      "algebra"
    ],
    "difficulty": 3,
