        "text": "4028"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "impossible to determine"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Add up angles",
        "body": "Let $T$ be the number of triangles. Their angles add up to $180^\\circ\\cdot T$. On the other hand, the angles around each of the 2013 inner points add up to $360^\\circ$, and the angles at the four corners of the square add up to $4\\cdot 90^\\circ = 360^\\circ$. So\n\n$$180T = 360\\cdot 2013 + 360 \\implies T = 2\\cdot 2013 + 2 = 4028.$$\n\n**Answer: (D) 4028**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Add points one at a time",
        "body": "With no inner points, a diagonal splits the square into 2 triangles. Adding an inner point inside a triangle splits it into 3 (net $+2$); one on a common edge splits two triangles into four (also net $+2$). So $n$ points give $2n + 2$ triangles: $4028$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 4028**"
      }
    ],
